  era: "Section 10 \xB7 Gupta Empire \xB7 c. 319 \u2013 550 CE"
  title: Gupta economy
  text: The Guptas issued the largest number of gold coins of any ancient Indian dynasty, called dinaras. Agriculture, crafts and guilds flourished, though some historians see a decline in long-distance trade with Rome and a rise in land grants.
